 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nSHOW TERSE statements not parsing correctly in Snowflake dialect\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing Snowflake SHOW statements with the TERSE modifier, the parser is not correctly identifying the TERSE keyword, causing incorrect parsing behavior.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\n\n# This should parse correctly but doesn't\nsql = \"SHOW TERSE TABLES IN SCHEMA db1.schema1\"\nast = parse_one(sql, read='snowflake')\nprint(ast)\n\n# Also affects other SHOW TERSE statements\nsql2 = \"SHOW TERSE SCHEMAS IN DATABASE db1\"\nast2 = parse_one(sql2, read='snowflake')\nprint(ast2)\n\nsql3 = \"SHOW TERSE PRIMARY KEYS IN TABLE foo\"\nast3 = parse_one(sql3, read='snowflake')\nprint(ast3)\n```\n\nThe TERSE modifier should be properly recognized and handled in SHOW statements, but it appears the parser is looking at the wrong token position to detect it.\n</issue>\n",
